==Latin==

===Etymology===
From root {{term|op}} in {{term|ops}}.<!-- Century 1911 says: from root "op" in "optare" ("to choose") -->

===Adjective===
'''optimus''' ''m'', '''[[optima]]''' ''f'', '''[[optimum]]''' ''n''

# best; irregular superlative of '''[[bonus]]''', ''good''.
#: ''Hic mundus perfectissimus est etiam mundorum possibilium omnium optimus'' : This most perfect world is even the best of all possible worlds ([[Immanuel Kant]], echoing Leibniz). [http://www.korpora.org/Kant/agb-metaphysica/II2.html]

